docs {
  # Code Sets Registry

  ## Concept Overview

  In SIF 3.7, the **Code Sets** utility service allows administrators to manage
  controlled vocabularies (code sets) within a solution. Code sets define allowed
  values for various fields.

  Code set management is admin-only for write operations (create, update, delete).
  Read operations (list, get by ID) are available to all authenticated environments.

  ## Test Purpose

  Verify that:
  1. Admin can create a code set (201)
  2. Code sets can be listed with SIF collection wrapper (200)
  3. A code set can be retrieved by ID (200)
  4. Admin can update a code set (200)
  5. Admin can delete a code set (204)
  6. Non-admin create/update/delete returns 403

  ## Prerequisites

  - This section is self-contained (creates its own domain/solution)

  ## SIF Specification Reference

  - SIF 3.7 Infrastructure — Utility Services — Code Sets
}

